# Testing and verification

## Commands

Run from the project root:

```powershell
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run test:unit
npm run test:operations
npm run test:integration
npm run test:stability
npm run build
npm run secrets:check
npm run evidence:check-phase1
npm run evidence:check-prior
npm run evidence:inventory
git diff --check
```

`npm test` is the fixture/unit suite, including local SQLite/OS operational tests. `test:operations` repeats its four operational files and is not additive to the complete unit count. Integration is isolated in `vitest.integration.config.ts` and requires access to the fixed public Pharos RPC and hosted MCP endpoints.

`npm run verify` runs 26 checks, including typecheck/lint/unit/operations/integration/stability/build, built CLI help, inspect/live-risk/historical-risk smokes, historical Phase 2 proof regression, two one-cycle monitor processes with restart/history/status checks, a 15-command operational CLI smoke, six oracle audit/status processes, source/runtime links, audit, archive/oracle integrity, exact typed Phase 2 replays, inventory, links, secret scan and Git whitespace checks. The dependent sequence stops on failure; preservation/inventory/scanning still run. Exact exit codes/times/output filenames are in `evidence/phase5/verification-results.json`, with unique transcripts/test snapshots under `verification-runs/`. Most subprocesses have a five-minute bound; monitor/operational harnesses have nine minutes and the oracle harness thirteen. Monitor/oracle smoke children have four-minute hard bounds; operational smoke children have three minutes.

The repository was initialized locally for Phase 1. Phase 5 preserves existing intent-to-add entries and uses `git diff --check` plus `git diff --no-index --check` for new files; it does not change the real Git index, commit or push. The current inventory is `docs/phase5-files.md`, with original/current hashes in `evidence/phase5/file-changes.json`. Prior completed inventories remain unchanged.

After documenting measured results, `npm run verify -- --finalize` repeats the five local inventory/link/secret/whitespace checks and confirms tested source/configuration/scripts are unchanged. It also fingerprints the documentation checked by that attempt. `npm run release:manifest` and `npm run release:check` require finalization after the completed full run, unchanged finalized documentation, and exact test-report copies from that run. The manifest binds runtime/source/build/documents/evidence, and release checking performs a read-only secret scan including the generated manifest/checksum. Any executable-input change requires a full run. See [reliability testing](reliability-testing.md) and [the final report](phase5-report.md#12-tests-and-exact-verification-results).

